When the GitHub step was skipped, its section is one line: `## GitHub — not checked: <reason>`.
Every item that needs me is also listed under **Needs your attention**.

## 8. Save
Skip this step for a report-only run or after a failed fetch.
1. If `.claude/notes/recap/.gitignore` doesn't exist, write it with the single line `*`: it keeps the
   folder (itself included) out of git, so the project's own `.gitignore` is never edited.
2. Write the report to `.claude/notes/recap/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`, today's date; if that file exists,
   add `-2`, `-3`, ….
3. Write `.claude/notes/recap/state.json` **last**, after the report — never for a `--since` run:
   `{"version": 1, "remote": "origin", "default": "<default>", "recorded_at": "<ISO 8601 time>", "github_checked_at": "<ISO 8601 time>", "tips": {"<branch>": "<full SHA>"}}`.
   Take each tip from the step 2 snapshot. Only branches you finished analyzing (or that didn't
   change) get their new tip; the rest keep their old one, and deleted branches drop out.
   `github_checked_at` is github.json's `fetched_at` when this run's answer says `"ok"`; otherwise
   keep the old value (or leave it out).
